# ============================================================================
# FEE3411 Publication/ — this is the git repo, and the site it builds is
# PUBLIC. Git history is permanent, so what is excluded here matters.
# ============================================================================

# ---- NEVER COMMIT ---------------------------------------------------------
# These never reach this folder — ./sync.sh does not copy them — but keep the
# rules as a backstop in case anything is ever placed here by hand.
#   Books/       the four copyrighted set texts
#   Attendance/  student personal data
Books/
Attendance/
*Attendance*.xlsx
src/Books/
src/Attendance/

# Marking schemes and tutorial solutions: not synced by default (see the note
# in sync.sh). Backstop only -- sync.sh should never produce these under src/,
# but if it (or a manual copy) ever does, this keeps them from being staged.
*marking-scheme*
*-solutions.pdf

# Internal planning documents.
FEE3411_Course_Spec.md
Claude outputs/
NOTES.md

# ---- generated by web/build_site.sh ---------------------------------------
# Rebuilt from src/ on every CI run; committing it would only cause conflicts.
# NOTE: docs/tutorials.md and docs/assignments.md are hand-written landing
# pages and stay committed -- only the docs/tutorials/ and docs/assignments/
# SUBDIRECTORIES (the individual generated tutorial/assignment pages) are
# generated, same pattern as docs/notes/ vs notes.md-that-doesn't-exist.
docs/notes/
docs/tutorials/
docs/assignments/
docs/supplementary/
docs/pdf/
build/
site_build/

# NOTE: src/ IS committed. It is the copy of the LaTeX sources that CI builds
# the site from — without it the GitHub Actions run has nothing to compile.

# ---- LaTeX build artefacts ------------------------------------------------
*.aux
*.log
*.fls
*.fdb_latexmk
*.out
*.toc
*.synctex.gz
*.tmp
tmp*.tmp

# ---- misc -----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
